sat13 check patch for Satsuma 4f73975c (tools/symext_probe.py, "check").

In fix mode Satsuma works in rounds. It starts the proof again at every round
with a fresh header and numbers the constraints against that round's formula:
clause i of the round's clause store is constraint i + 1, and what the round
derives comes after. The deletions of a later round therefore name clauses by
their place in that round's formula, not by their number in the proof so far,
and one VeriPB stream over the whole file deletes the wrong clauses. This
patch writes each round's formula, in the store's order, to
$SATSUMA_ROUND_DUMP.<round>.cnf when that variable is set, so the checker can
renumber every round. Nothing else changes: the output and the proof are the
same bytes with or without it (the check compares the output with the one
measured).

Apply to a copy of the audited tree, never to the measured binary's tree:
    patch -p1 -d ~/.cache/sat13-tools/satsuma-rounds < tools/satsuma-round-dump.patch

--- a/src/satsuma.h
+++ b/src/satsuma.h
@@ -8,6 +8,9 @@
 #define SATSUMA_VERSION_MAJOR 1
 #define SATSUMA_VERSION_MINOR 4

+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <string>
 #include "dejavu/ds.h"
 #include "dejavu/dejavu.h"
 #include "cnf.h"
@@ -672,6 +675,20 @@
                 if(my_proof) my_proof->set_proof_dense_crossover(proof_dense_crossover);
                 if(my_proof) my_proof->set_pol_logging(proof_pol_log);
                 if(my_proof) my_proof->header(formula.n_clauses());
+                // sat13 check patch: the round's formula, clause i being constraint i + 1
+                if(my_proof && std::getenv("SATSUMA_ROUND_DUMP")) {
+                    const std::string dump_name = std::string(std::getenv("SATSUMA_ROUND_DUMP")) + "." +
+                                                  std::to_string(iteration) + ".cnf";
+                    std::ofstream dump(dump_name);
+                    dump << "p cnf " << formula.n_variables() << " " << formula.n_clauses() << "\n";
+                    for(int i = 0; i < formula.n_clauses(); ++i) {
+                        for(int j = 0; j < formula.clause_size(i); ++j)
+                            dump << formula.literal_at_clause_pos(i, j) << " ";
+                        dump << "0\n";
+                    }
+                    dump.close();
+                    if(!dump) terminate_with_error("unable to write the round dump '" + dump_name + "'");
+                }

